$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure (3) for the synthesis of 1,4-diazepinones 5a-d
Homoallylic ketone 4 (1 equiv) was stirred in a 1:1 TFA/ DCM solution for
30 minutes. After removal of the volatiles under vacuum, the residue was
placed for 1 hour under vacum (5 mm Hg) to remove excess TFA. The residue
was dissolved in DCM (c = 10- 3 M), cooled to 0 °C, treated with
triethylamine (1.1 mmol), stirred for 20 minutes, treated with 4 Å
molecular sieves, stirred 15 minutes, treated with sodium
triacetoxyborohydride (2 to 3 equiv) in two portions and stirred for 3 to
5 days at room temperature under argon atmosphere. The mixture was
filtered, the filtrate was concentrated on a rotary evaporator, and
partitioned between saturated aqueous NaHCO3 solution and ethyl acetate.
The aqueous was separated and extracted with ethyl acetate (3x 10ml). The
combined organic phase was dried over magnesium sulphate, filtered and
evaporated to a residue, that was purified further as specified. (3S,
5S)-5-(But-3-enyl)-3-methyl-1,4-diazepin-2-one (5a) : The residue was
purified by reverse-phase HPLC to afford diazepinone 5a as a colorless
oil (28 mg, 45% yield). colorless oil. Rf 0.24 (5 % methanol in
chloroform). 1H NMR (300 MHz, MeOD) δ 1.47 (d, 3 H, J = 6.9), 1.61 (m, 2
H), 2.0 (m, 2 H), 2.22 (m, 2 H), 3.30-3.32 (m, 2 H), 3.47-3.52 (m, 2 H),
4.31 (q, 1 H, J = 6.6), 5.08 (m, 2 H), 5.82 (m, 1 H). 13C NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3), δ 170.4, 136.7, 115.6, 61.9, 54.6, 48.8, 38.8, 33.0, 29.3, 14.4.
HRMS (EI) m/z 205.1311 [M+Na+; calcd for C10H18N2ONa: 205.1313]. [α]D 20
= +3.9 ° (c 0.007, MeOH).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM 4A mol. sieves added stage 3
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM 1,4-Diazepinone and Pyrrolodiazepinone Syntheses via Homoallylic Ketones
from Cascade Addition of Vinyl Grignard Reagent to α-Aminoacyl-β-amino
Esters
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Iden, Hassan S.; Lubell, William D.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
