$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Method E:
4-Morpholino-1-phenylsulfonyl-1'-allyl-5'-methyl-2,2'-bipyrrole. A
solution of TiCl4 1M in toluene (430 μL, 0.431 mmol) was added dropwise
to dione (140 mg, 0.359 mmol) and allylamine (54 μL, 0.718 mmol) in
toluene (15 mL). After stirring for 18 h, the reaction was treated with a
solution of saturated aqueous NH4Cl followed by 20 mwere separated and
the aqueous layer was extracted with EtOAc (15 mL x 2) and CHCl 3 (15
mL). The organic layers were combined, washed with brine, dried (MgSO4)
and concentrated to a residue that was purified by column chromatography
on silica gel (45 % ethyl acetate/hexane). Evaporation of the collected
fractions.
4-Methoxy-1-phenylsulfonyl-1'-[2-(phenylthio)ethyl]-5'-methyl-2,2'-bipyrrole
as a red foam, yield 25 mg, 37 %. 1H NMR (400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.55-7.211H),
6.01 (d, J = 2.1 Hz, 1H), 5.86 (d, J = 3.4 Hz, 1H), 5.73 (d, J = 3.4 Hz,
1H), 3.80 (m, 5H), 2.90 (m, 2H), 2.20 (s, 3H); (m, 10H), 6.89 (d, J = 2.1
Hz, 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 150.2, 138.1, 133.5, 130.2, 129.5, 129.0,
128.9, 128.6, 127.4, 126.3, 125.9, 120.3, 112.4, 111.2, 106.3, 103.1,
57.5, 44.0, 33.0, 12.5. HRMS Calcd for C24H25N2O3S2 [M+H+] 453.1301,
found 453.1308.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM 4-Alkoxy- and 4-amino-2,2'-bipyrrole synthesis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Jolicoeur, Benoit; Lubell, William D.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2006), 8(26), 6107-6110

