$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General/Typical Procedure:
1-(2-(Chloromethyl)-3-methylphenyl)-1H-pyrrole (Table 2, entry 2):
Prepared by the same procedures with (Table 1, entry 1) substrate
(Procedure A) on page S10-11; Methyl 2-amino-6-methylbenzoate (991 mg ,
6.0 mmol) was used instead of 2-aminobenzoate. Furthermore, in Paal-
Knorr pyrrole synthesis step, only AcOH was employed as a solvent and
refluxed for 1 h to obtained the methyl
2-methyl-6-(1H-pyrrol-1-yl)benzoate. The desired adduct was obtained 777
mg (63%) in 3 steps; (EtOAc/n-hexane, 1:15); colorless oil; To an
oven-dried two-neck round bottom flask (150 mL), a solution of lithium
aluminum hydride (1.0 M in diethyl ether, 20 mL, 20 mmol) was added to Sa
(1.9 g, 9.5 mmol) in diethyl ether (20 mL) at 0 °C. The reaction mixture
was warmed to room temperature and then stirred for 1 h. The sodium
sulfate decahydrate (4.0 g) was slowly added to quench the reaction at 0
°C, and stirred for additional 20 min. The reaction mixture was diluted
with EtOAc (10 mL), filtered through a plug of celite, and eluted with
additional EtOAc (40 mL). The filtrate was concentrated in vacuo and the
crude residue was purified by flash column chromatography
(EtOAc/n-hexane, 1:3) to afford (2-(1H-pyrrol-1-yl)phenyl)methanol, Sb
(1.53 g, 93%); white solid; To a solution of Sb (693 mg, 4 mmol) in
CH2Cl2 (12 mL) was added Et3N (0.826 mL, 6.0 mmol) in one portion at room
temprature followed by the addition of methane sulfonyl chloride (0.373
mL, 4.8 mmol). The reaction mixture was stirred for 12 h, concentrated in
vacuo, and purified by silica gel column chromatography (EtOAc/n-hexane,
1:10) to afford Sc (558 mg, 75%); colorless oil;
1-(2-(Chloromethyl)phenyl)-2-methyl-1H-pyrrole (Table 2, entry 11):
Prepared by the same procedures with (Table 1, entry 1) substrate
(Procedure A) on page S10-11; 4-oxopentanal4 was used instead of
2,5-dimethoxytetrahydrofuran for Paal-Knorr pyrrole synthesis. The
desired adduct was obtained 181 mg (17%) in 3 steps; 1H NMR (400 MHz,
CDCl3) δ 7.61 (dd, J = 7.6, 1.7 Hz, 1H), 7.44 (m, 2H), 7.25 (dd, J = 7.5,
1.4 Hz, 1H), 6.67 (t, J = 2.3Hz, 1H), 6.22 (t, J = 3.1 Hz, 1H), 6.04 (m,
1H), 4.30 (d, J = 15.4 Hz, 1H), 2.02 (s, 3H); 13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ
138.8, 135.6, 130.6, 129.8, 129.0, 128.8, 128.6, 121.8, 108.1, 107.2,
41.3, 12.1; IR (Film) ν 2916, 1500, 1457, 1414, 1326, 1086, 1027, 767,
705 cm-1; HRMS (EI+) m/z calcd. for C12H12ClN [M]+: 205.0658, found:
205.0659.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Paal-Knorr reaction in first stage
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
