$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Methyl
5-tert-butyl-2-(2-phenyethyl)furane-3-carboxylate. 12 Product 5 (0.5 g,
1,64 mmol) was dissolved into EtOH (2 mL) into a 50 mL roundbottom flask
equipped with a stir bar and a reflux condenser. HCl 0.1 mL of a 37%
solution) was added and the flask inserted into the cavity of a Discovery
Microwave System apparatus (from CEM) and heated at 150 W for 4 min
(internal temperature 100°C). The mixture was diluted with AcOEt and the
solvent washed several times with a saturated solution of NaHCO3. The
organic layer was dried over anhydrous Na2SO4 and the solvent evaporated.
The 1H NMR spectrum of the crude showed the presence of pure furan 10
that could be eventually additionally purified by flash chromatography
(eluent Hexane: AcOEt 8: 1, Rf = 0.75). Obtained 0.49 g, 95% yield. 1H
NMR spectrum enclosed. compound 13.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM microwave irradiation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Microwave-assisted Paal-Knorr reaction. A rapid approach to substituted
pyrroles and furans
