$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 1.2 General method of Paal-Knorr reaction
2,5-Hexanedione 3.0 mmol, amine 3.0 mmol and formic acid 0.45 mmol were
added to a 50 mL round-bottom flask successively, then stirred for 0.5-6
h at room temperature, and traced by TLC. After reaction, the mixture was
washed with cold saturated NaHCO3 solution (15 mL × 2) and ice water (15
mL × 3) successively, then placed in a vacuum dryer with anhydrous
calcium chloride at room temperature to give the pure compound 3a-3k. 3m
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
