$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM 1-Ethyl-2,5-bis(4-methoxyphenyl)-3,4-di(naphthalen-2-yl)-1H-pyrrole
(11b). Compound 8 (2.5 g, 4.5 mmol) and ammonium acetate (7 g, 90.8 mmol)
were dissolved in 14mL of acetic acid in a 250 mL two-neck round-bottom
flask that was equipped with a reflux condenser, a magnetic stirrer, and
a hot plate. The mixed solution was refluxed for 36 h. After the reaction
had run to completion, the solution was poured into icy deionic water,
and white powder precipitated out.
2,5-Bis(4-methoxyphenyl)-3,4-di(naphthalen-2-yl)furan (10). Compound 10
(10-20%) was obtained as a byproduct in the synthesis of compound 11a
(acid-catalyzed Parr-Knorr furan condensation). 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3,
δ) 3.78 (s, 6H), 6.80 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 4H), 7.29 (d, J = 8.4 Hz, 2H),
7.36-7.44 (m, 4H), 7.48 (d, J = 8.7 Hz, 4H), 7.60-7.72 (m, 6H), 7.78 (d,
J = 7.8 Hz, 2H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3, δ) 55.1, 113.8, 123.3, 123.8,
125.8, 125.8, 127.3, 127.6, 127.9, 127.9, 128.6, 129.2, 131.0, 132.3,
133.4, 147.7, 158.8; HRMS (FAB) m/z calcd for C38H28O3 532.2038, found
532.2044 (M+).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Paal-Knorr reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
